        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1f45c87f-4171-5235-9a29-1c5355128648",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Kolles, Romulus Kolles\n- Organizations: Hispania Racing F1 Team, Jordan Grand Prix, Midland F1, Spyker F1 Team, Force India, ByKolles Racing\n- Places: Timişoara, Romania\n- Events: 2007 Formula One World Championship\n- Topics: Formula One, German Formula 3, F3 Euro Series\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Kolles was born as Călin Colesnic on 13 December 1967 in Timişoara, Romania.\n- ByKolles Racing was founded in 2000 by Romulus Kolles and his son Colin Kolles as Kolles Racing.\n- ByKolles Racing initially competed in German Formula 3 before moving to the F3 Euro Series from 2003 to 2005.\n- Colin Kolles held a team principal and managing director role at the Formula One team known as Jordan, Midland, Spyker, and Force India from 2005 to 2008.\n- Spyker F1 Team was created by Spyker Cars after buying the short-lived Midland F1 team, which had previously been Jordan Grand Prix.\n- Spyker F1 Team, also called the Etihad Aldar Spyker F1 Team for sponsorship reasons, competed in the 2007 Formula One World Championship.\n- At the end of the 2007 season, Spyker F1 Team was sold and renamed Force India.\n- Colin Kolles later became the former team principal and managing director of the Hispania Racing F1 Team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7f673771-fbb3-5266-9a9a-c8bacca6dc86",
        "text": "Page: Colin Kolles. Sentence: Colin Kolles (born Călin Colesnic 13 December 1967 in Timişoara, Romania) is the former team principal and managing director of the Hispania Racing F1 Team, previously holding a similar position at the team known under the names Jordan, Midland, Spyker and Force India from 2005 to 2008.\nPage: Spyker F1. Sentence: The Spyker F1 Team, known as the Etihad Aldar Spyker F1 Team for sponsorship reasons was a Formula One team that competed in the 2007 Formula One World Championship, and was created by Spyker Cars after their buyout of the short-lived Midland F1 (formerly Jordan Grand Prix) team.\nPage: Spyker F1. Sentence: At the end of the 2007 season the team was sold and renamed Force India.\nPage: ByKolles Racing. Sentence: Founded in 2000 by Romulus Kolles and his son Colin Kolles as Kolles Racing, the company initially participated in German Formula 3 before moving to the F3 Euro Series from 2003 to 2005.",
